# OpsPick brand logo

## Source of truth

- Master mark: `branding/opspick-logo-1024.png`
- App Store 1024: `branding/app-store-icon-1024.png`
- Web UI: `frontend/public/branding/opspick-logo.png` via `OpsPickLogo` / `/branding/opspick-logo.png`
- Mobile UI: `mobile/assets/branding/opspick-logo.png` (+ `opspick_logo.png` alias)
  - Use `OpsPickLogo` from `mobile/lib/core/branding/opspick_logo.dart`
  - Declare folder in `mobile/pubspec.yaml`: `assets/branding/`
  - After changing assets: `flutter pub get` then **full restart** (hot reload does not pick up new assets)
- iOS launcher: `mobile/ios/Runner/Assets.xcassets/AppIcon.appiconset/`
- Android launcher: `mobile/android/app/src/main/res/mipmap-*/ic_launcher*.png`

When replacing the logo, regenerate all of the above from the master 1024 PNG. Do not revive `mobile/assets/app_icon_source.svg` (old orange clipboard).

## App Store Connect — why the grid placeholder shows

ASC **cannot** be updated from this repo. The Apps list wireframe grid means no processed icon/build yet.

### Option A (recommended): upload a new iOS build

1. Archive & upload a build that includes the updated `AppIcon.appiconset` (esp. `Icon-App-1024x1024@1x.png`).
2. App Store Connect → Apps → Mini Task Manager (or OpsPick) → version → select the new build.
3. After processing, the Apps list and app detail replace the grid with the logo.

### Option B: manual 1024 upload

1. Open [App Store Connect](https://appstoreconnect.apple.com) → Apps → the app.
2. App Information (or the version App Store tab).
3. Upload `branding/app-store-icon-1024.png` (exactly 1024×1024 PNG; flatten/remove alpha if Apple rejects it).

Optional: rename listing display name from “Mini Task Manager” → **OpsPick** under App Information.
